     "Scripture: Hebrews 12:1–3",
     "The testimony of faithful believers can encourage others to persevere, while the passage directs attention to Jesus.",
     "Kingdom principle: Learn from the faithfulness of others, but keep Christ at the center of your devotion.",
     "10. Build a Legacy Through Discipleship",
     "Scripture: 2 Timothy 2:2",
     "The Christian message is intended to be passed on through faithful people who can teach others.",
     "Kingdom principle: Measure your legacy not only by what you accomplish but also by the people you help grow in faith, wisdom, and responsibility.",
     "Peer-to-Peer Group Reflection",
     "These questions can be used for a P2P Global Bible study, discipleship circle, or personal reflection.",
     "Discussion 1: Early Christianity and Discipleship",
     "1. What challenges did the early Church face as the first generation of apostles passed away?",
     "2. Why was it important to preserve the teaching of Jesus?",
     "3. What can Polycarp’s place in early Christian history teach us about discipleship?",
     "4. How can we pass the Christian faith to the next generation responsibly?",
     "Discussion 2: Leadership and Character",
     "1. What responsibilities did Polycarp have as bishop of Smyrna?",
     "2. Why must Christian leaders demonstrate the character they teach?",
     "3. What qualities help a leader serve a church faithfully?",
     "4. How can a Christian community maintain accountability for its leaders?",
     "Discussion 3: Truth and Christian Conduct",
     "1. Why did early Christian leaders need to respond to competing teachings?",
     "2. How can believers defend their convictions without becoming arrogant?",
     "3. Why should Christians distinguish biblical teaching from personal preference?",
     "4. How can churches help members develop sound judgment?",
     "Discussion 4: Faith Under Pressure",
     "1. What pressures could Christians face within Roman society?",
     "2. What does the message to Smyrna in Revelation 2:8–11 teach about perseverance?",
     "3. Why is Polycarp remembered for his response to the Roman authorities?",
     "4. How can believers remain faithful when doing what is right becomes costly?",
     "Discussion 5: Martyrdom and Historical Memory",
     "1. What does the word martyr mean in Christian history?",
     "2. Why is The Martyrdom of Polycarp an important historical source?",
     "3. Why should ancient accounts be studied with both respect and critical judgment?",
     "4. How can the testimony of earlier Christians encourage believers today without encouraging unnecessary risk?",
     "Discussion 6: Personal Faithfulness and Legacy",
     "1. What are the most important lessons from Polycarp’s life?",
     "2. Why is daily faithfulness important before a crisis occurs?",
     "3. How can we help others develop a stronger understanding of Scripture?",
     "4. What kind of Christian example do we want to leave for the next generation?",
     "5. What practical change can we make this week to grow in faithfulness?",
     "Group Activity: The Polycarp Faithfulness Review",
