     "• •\tGroup C: Polycarp’s arrest, trial, and refusal to renounce Christ.",
     "• •\tGroup D: Polycarp’s legacy and the lessons of Christian perseverance.",
     "Each group should identify:",
     "1. Three important events or historical details.",
     "2. Two qualities demonstrated in Polycarp’s life or teaching.",
     "3. Two challenges faced by the early Christian community.",
     "4. Three practical lessons for Christians today.",
     "5. One question about Polycarp’s story that requires further historical or biblical investigation.",
     "Have each group present its findings. Conclude by discussing how Christians can honour faithful believers from the past while keeping Jesus Christ at the center of their faith."
