   "Afterward, write a short reflection explaining:",
   "1. What you did.",
   "2. Why you chose that action.",
   "3. How it helped the person or group.",
   "4. What you learned about Christian service.",
   "5. What you could do differently next time.",
   "Completion Commitment",
   "Complete the following statement in your own words:",
   "“Because I have learned from Justin Martyr’s life, I will seek truth by __________, grow in my understanding of Jesus Christ by __________, and serve others through __________.”",
   "Memory Verse",
   "1 Peter 3:15 (KJV)",
   "“But sanctify the Lord God in your hearts: and be ready always to give an answer to every man that asketh you a reason of the hope that is in you with meekness and fear:”",
   "Memory Verse Reflection",
   "This passage connects closely with Justin Martyr’s life.",
   "He believed that Christians should be prepared to explain the hope they had found in Jesus Christ. He used his knowledge, writing, and teaching to address questions about the Christian faith.",
   "However, the verse also teaches that our witness must be accompanied by humility and respect.",
   "Being prepared to explain our beliefs does not mean we should become proud, aggressive, or dismissive of other people.",
   "We are called to understand what we believe, communicate it faithfully, and treat others with the dignity they deserve.",
   "Personal application: Memorize this verse and consider how you can become better prepared to explain your Christian hope with wisdom, gentleness, and respect.",
   "Closing Prayer",
   "Heavenly Father,",
   "Thank You for the life and example of Justin Martyr, who searched for truth, discovered the significance of Jesus Christ, and devoted his abilities to explaining and defending the Christian faith.",
   "Give me a sincere desire to know You more deeply. Teach me not to be satisfied with superficial understanding, but to study Your Word carefully and grow in wisdom.",
   "Help me to ask honest questions, listen patiently, and remain humble when I discover that I do not know everything.",
