     "Do not settle for superficial answers to the deepest questions of life. Study carefully, ask honest questions, and remain willing to learn.",
     "2. Make Jesus Christ central",
     "Christianity is not merely a collection of moral principles or philosophical ideas. Its center is Jesus Christ, His identity, His work, and His resurrection.",
     "3. Use knowledge to serve others",
     "Education and intellectual ability should not become tools for pride. They can be used to explain truth, strengthen others, and contribute to the common good.",
     "4. Learn to explain your faith",
     "A believer should be willing to learn Scripture and communicate Christian convictions clearly. We do not need to know everything, but we should remain committed to growing in understanding.",
