     "As Christianity spread, it encountered different cultures, philosophies, religious traditions, and explanations of spiritual reality.",
     "People asked important questions.",
     "Who is God?",
     "Why does evil exist?",
     "What is the relationship between the physical world and the spiritual world?",
     "Who exactly is Jesus Christ?",
     "How does humanity receive salvation?",
     "These questions were not unimportant. They concerned the central meaning of Christian faith.",
     "However, not every answer offered in the name of Christianity agreed with the message proclaimed by the apostles.",
     "Different teachers developed explanations of Jesus Christ and salvation that departed from the beliefs held by many early Christian communities.",
     "Some movements associated with Gnosticism emphasized special spiritual knowledge. Certain teachers distinguished sharply between the highest God and the creator of the material world. Others presented interpretations of Jesus that challenged the Church’s confession of His genuine humanity.",
     "It is important to recognize that Gnosticism was not one completely uniform movement. Different groups held different beliefs, and historians continue to study their origins, development, and relationship to early Christianity.",
     "Nevertheless, Irenaeus believed that some of these teachings seriously distorted the gospel.",
     "The issue was not simply that Christians disagreed about minor details. The disagreements concerned the identity of God, the nature of creation, the person of Jesus Christ, and the meaning of salvation.",
     "If the creator of the world were not the true God, what would that mean for the biblical account of creation?",
     "If Jesus had not genuinely become human, what would that mean for His suffering, death, and resurrection?",
     "If salvation depended on secret knowledge available only to a select group, what would that mean for the public proclamation of the gospel?",
     "Irenaeus recognized that such questions required serious attention.",
