     "The Church today faces a similar responsibility. People encounter many competing messages about God, spirituality, identity, salvation, and the meaning of life.",
     "Some teachings may use Christian language while changing the meaning of central Christian beliefs.",
     "Believers therefore need discernment: the ability to examine ideas carefully and distinguish truth from error.",
     "Irenaeus’s life demonstrates that discernment is not the same as suspicion toward everything unfamiliar. It involves understanding what is being taught, examining the evidence, and comparing the teaching with the gospel."
