     "It told one unfolding story of God’s relationship with humanity.",
     "In the beginning, God created the world and made human beings in His image. Humanity was created for life with God, but sin disrupted that relationship.",
     "God did not abandon His creation. Throughout history, He continued working toward the restoration of humanity.",
     "The covenants, the prophets, the coming of Christ, His death and resurrection, and the promise of future renewal belonged to this one divine purpose.",
     "Irenaeus rejected explanations that divided God’s work into competing or unrelated plans.",
     "He believed that salvation was not an escape from a creation that God had failed to make properly. Instead, salvation was God’s work of overcoming sin and death and bringing humanity into the life He intended.",
     "This vision gave Christian hope a broad scope.",
     "God’s purpose was not merely to rescue isolated individuals from the consequences of their sins. It also involved the restoration of humanity under the lordship of Jesus Christ and the fulfillment of God’s purposes for creation.",
