     "For many people in the Roman Empire, religion was closely connected to family traditions, civic identity, and public life.",
     "Religious ceremonies were not always viewed as private expressions of personal belief. They could also be understood as ways of showing loyalty to a city, honoring its traditions, and maintaining the favor of the gods.",
