     "They refused to worship the traditional Roman gods and would not treat the emperor as a deity. Their refusal could be interpreted as disrespect toward society or as a rejection of established customs.",
     "This created suspicion.",
     "Some outsiders misunderstood Christian gatherings. Others repeated accusations without understanding what Christians actually believed or practised.",
     "Christian communities could be accused of immoral behavior, disloyalty, or secret activities. Such accusations varied by place and circumstance, and Christians did not experience persecution uniformly throughout the empire.",
     "Nevertheless, the possibility of hostility remained a serious concern.",
     "Tertullian believed that Christians should not be condemned simply because they were Christians.",
     "He argued that accusations should be examined rather than accepted merely because they were popular.",
     "If Christians were accused of crimes, the authorities should establish whether those crimes had actually been committed. A person’s religious identity should not replace a fair examination of the evidence.",
     "This principle was central to his defense of Christianity.",
     "Tertullian wanted his readers to recognize the difference between genuine wrongdoing and prejudice against a group because of its beliefs.",
     "His arguments were especially important because Christians could find themselves in a vulnerable position when their religious identity became the basis of suspicion.",
     "The issue was not that Christians should be exempt from the law. Rather, Tertullian argued that they should be judged fairly, according to their actual conduct and the evidence presented against them.",
     "His writing challenges Christians today to think carefully about justice.",
     "When people are misunderstood because of their religion, ethnicity, nationality, or convictions, the appropriate response is not to spread further prejudice. It is to seek truth, fairness, and justice.",
