     "One of his most influential works was the Apology, generally dated to around AD 197.",
     "In this work, Tertullian addressed Roman readers and challenged the treatment of Christians. He argued that Christians should not be punished merely for bearing the Christian name.",
     "He also explained aspects of Christian worship and community life, challenging the idea that Christian gatherings were the criminal activities that some critics alleged.",
     "Tertullian wanted people to understand that Christians gathered to worship God, pray, study, and support one another.",
     "He argued that Christian morality and community life should be judged according to what Christians actually did, not according to rumors about what outsiders imagined they did.",
     "His approach reflected a larger conviction: truth should not fear honest examination.",
     "Tertullian did not assume that every criticism of Christianity was automatically correct. Nor did he believe that accusations should be accepted without evidence.",
     "Instead, he challenged his readers to examine the claims being made and consider whether they were justified.",
