    "title": "The Complexity of Tertullian’s Later Life",
    "scripture": "",
    "narrative": [
     "Tertullian’s influence on Christian writing was considerable, but his life was not without controversy.",
     "During his later years, he became associated with the New Prophecy movement, commonly called Montanism.",
     "The movement emerged in Phrygia in Asia Minor during the second century and was associated with Montanus and the prophetesses Priscilla and Maximilla.",
     "Its followers emphasized prophetic activity and a serious expectation of God’s work in the life of the Church.",
     "The movement also became associated with demanding standards of Christian discipline.",
     "Tertullian appears to have embraced its more rigorous tendencies, although the precise stages of his relationship with the movement are debated by scholars.",
     "His later writings reveal a strong concern with repentance, moral discipline, marriage, fasting, and the seriousness of Christian conduct.",
     "These concerns reflected his conviction that Christian discipleship should involve genuine transformation rather than superficial religious identification.",
     "However, his association with the New Prophecy movement complicated his relationship with the wider Church.",
     "The history of this movement involved disagreements about prophecy, authority, discipline, and the life of Christian communities.",
     "It would therefore be misleading to present every aspect of Tertullian’s later position as universally accepted Christian teaching.",
     "His life offers an important lesson in historical discernment.",
     "A person can make significant contributions to Christian thought while also holding positions that later Christians question or reject.",
     "We should neither ignore a person’s valuable contributions simply because the person was controversial, nor accept every teaching merely because the person was influential.",
     "Each teaching must be examined carefully.",
     "This principle is especially important in an age when believers can become strongly attached to particular preachers, authors, ministries, or online personalities.",
     "Respect for a teacher should never eliminate the responsibility to evaluate what that teacher says.",
     "Likewise, disagreement with a teacher should not prevent us from recognizing genuine insights or useful contributions.",
     "Tertullian’s later life reminds us that Christian history is complex and that spiritual discernment requires both appreciation and careful evaluation."
    ],
