     "text": "1. What did Origen’s life become known for?\nA. Avoiding all study\nB. Intellectual work and serious Christian discipline\nC. Political conquest\nD. Building a military empire\n2. According to 1 Corinthians 9:24–27, what can athletic training illustrate?\nA. The importance of discipline and perseverance\nB. The need to avoid all responsibility\nC. The superiority of physical strength over character\nD. The uselessness of practice\n3. What is the proper purpose of spiritual discipline?\nA. To make others feel inferior\nB. To prove that a person is better than everyone else\nC. To support growth, faithfulness, and service\nD. To avoid relationships with other believers\n4. True or False: The most extreme spiritual practice is always the most faithful one.\n5. Short Answer: Describe two habits that can help a Christian become a more disciplined student of Scripture.\n6. Personal Application: Create a simple weekly Bible-study schedule that you can realistically maintain."
