     "text": "1. During whose reign did the major persecution associated with Origen’s final suffering occur?\nA. Emperor Decius\nB. Emperor Constantine\nC. Emperor Theodosius I\nD. Emperor Justinian\n2. Around when did Origen die?\nA. AD 33\nB. AD 100\nC. AD 253–254\nD. AD 451\n3. What should Christians remember about suffering and theological correctness?\nA. Suffering proves every belief is correct\nB. Suffering is irrelevant to every historical question\nC. A person’s suffering and the accuracy of their teachings are separate questions\nD. Persecution always produces perfect understanding\n4. True or False: Remembering historical persecution should encourage concern for people who suffer for their faith today.\n5. Short Answer: Explain two ways a Christian community can support persecuted believers.\n6. Personal Application: Write a prayer for Christians who face imprisonment, violence, or discrimination because of their faith."
