     "Education can prepare us for a life of service. Knowledge becomes especially valuable when it is used to help others.",
     "Spiritual growth can develop over time. A person’s early interests do not necessarily determine the final direction of their life.",
     "Language matters when studying Scripture. Understanding the original languages can help readers examine biblical meaning more carefully.",
     "Intellectual ability requires purpose. Skills and knowledge should be directed toward work that benefits others.",
     "Serious learning requires discipline. Important achievements often grow from years of patient study."
