     "The Vulgate was not produced in a single moment by one person translating every biblical book from beginning to end.",
     "Latin biblical translations existed before Jerome. His work included revising the Latin Gospels and translating much of the Old Testament from Hebrew. Other parts of the Latin Bible had different histories, and the final form of the Vulgate developed through a broader process of transmission and revision.",
     "Nevertheless, Jerome’s contribution was central to its development.",
     "His scholarship gave Latin-speaking Christians access to a biblical text shaped by careful comparison of manuscripts and attention to the languages in which the Scriptures had originally been written.",
