     "Poetry relies on imagery, rhythm, and parallel expressions. Historical narratives may include unfamiliar customs and geographical details. Prophetic writings can contain symbolic language and difficult expressions. Letters require attention to argument, grammar, and the relationship between the writer and the original audience.",
