     "text": "PART A — MULTIPLE-CHOICE QUESTIONS\n1. In which city did Cyprian serve as bishop?\nA. Alexandria\nB. Carthage\nC. Rome\nD. Antioch\n2. What was Cyprian’s profession before his Christian conversion?\nA. Soldier\nB. Physician\nC. Rhetorician\nD. Merchant\n3. Around when did Cyprian become bishop of Carthage?\nA. AD 150\nB. AD 200\nC. AD 248–249\nD. AD 325\n4. Which Roman emperor was associated with the persecution that began in AD 250?\nA. Constantine\nB. Decius\nC. Theodosius\nD. Nero\n5. What did the term lapsi refer to in the controversies Cyprian addressed?\nA. Christians who had abandoned their communities permanently\nB. Christians who had failed or compromised during persecution\nC. Roman officials who became bishops\nD. Missionaries sent outside the empire\n6. Which work did Cyprian write about the unity of the Church?\nA. The City of God\nB. On the Incarnation\nC. On the Unity of the Catholic Church\nD. Confessions\n7. Which crisis became an important subject of Cyprian’s treatise On Mortality?\nA. A famine in Jerusalem\nB. An epidemic affecting the Roman world\nC. The fall of Constantinople\nD. The destruction of the Jerusalem temple\n8. What did Cyprian emphasize in On Works and Alms?\nA. Military service as the highest Christian duty\nB. The rejection of all education\nC. Generosity and care for people in need\nD. The necessity of political office\n9. Which bishop disagreed with Cyprian over rebaptizing people who had received baptism outside the Church’s recognized communion?\nA. Stephen of Rome\nB. Ambrose of Milan\nC. Augustine of Hippo\nD. Gregory of Nyssa\n10. In what year was Cyprian executed?\nA. AD 202\nB. AD 250\nC. AD 258\nD. AD 313\nPART B — SHORT-ANSWER QUESTIONS\n1. Describe Cyprian’s life before his conversion to Christianity.\n2. Why was Cyprian’s appointment as bishop significant?\n3. Explain the pressure Christians faced under Emperor Decius.\n4. Why did the restoration of the lapsed become controversial?\n5. What was Cyprian’s main concern in On the Unity of the Catholic Church?\n6. What themes did Cyprian address in On Mortality?\n7. Why was generosity important in Cyprian’s teaching?\n8. Explain the controversy between Cyprian and Stephen of Rome over baptism.\n9. What happened to Cyprian during the persecution under Valerian?\n10. What is one important lesson Christians can learn from Cyprian’s life?\nPART C — DEEPER REFLECTION QUESTIONS\n1. Cyprian changed direction after his conversion. How can a person’s abilities and experience be redirected toward serving God and others?\nSuggested Reflection: People may use their education, professional skills, influence, or resources to serve their communities. Christian growth involves considering not only personal advancement but also how those abilities can contribute to the good of others.\n2. How should a Christian community respond when members fail under pressure?\nSuggested Reflection: A community should take wrongdoing seriously while allowing for honest repentance and appropriate restoration. It should avoid both careless acceptance and permanent rejection without consideration of repentance, accountability, and the person’s circumstances.\n3. What can Cyprian’s concern for church unity teach communities experiencing conflict today?\nSuggested Reflection: Unity requires more than avoiding difficult conversations. It involves truthfulness, humility, mutual responsibility, and a willingness to seek reconciliation. Leaders should address genuine problems without encouraging unnecessary division.\n4. How can Christian hope help people face death without minimizing grief?\nSuggested Reflection: Christian hope points toward God’s promises and the resurrection, while allowing people to grieve the loss of loved ones. Faith should bring comfort and support rather than pressure people to hide their sorrow.\n5. What does generosity reveal about a person’s understanding of Christian discipleship?\nSuggested Reflection: Generosity can reveal whether someone sees possessions only as private benefits or also as resources that can help others. Genuine generosity should be offered with respect and compassion rather than as a means of gaining recognition.\n6. What does Cyprian’s disagreement with Stephen of Rome teach us about the history of Christian doctrine?\nSuggested Reflection: Early Christian leaders sometimes reached different conclusions about important questions. Studying those disagreements encourages careful examination of historical sources, fair representation of differing positions, and humility in theological discussion.\n7. What is the difference between seeking suffering and remaining faithful when suffering comes?\nSuggested Reflection: Seeking suffering unnecessarily can place oneself or others at avoidable risk. Remaining faithful means holding to important convictions with courage and wisdom when circumstances make faithfulness costly."
