     "The controversy also became entangled with political authority. Constantine, the emperor who had recently supported Christianity, wanted religious peace throughout his empire.",
     "For Constantine, a major dispute among Christians threatened the unity he hoped to establish. For the bishops, the question concerned the Church’s confession of Christ.",
