     "Key Scripture: John 1:1–3",
     "2. Christian Doctrine Must Be Examined Carefully",
     "The bishops sought language that would express their understanding of Scripture and distinguish their position from competing interpretations.",
     "Key Scripture: 2 Timothy 2:15",
     "3. Church Unity Requires More Than Agreement on the Surface",
     "The council adopted a common confession, but disagreement continued for decades. Lasting unity requires teaching, understanding, and responsible relationships.",
     "Key Scripture: Ephesians 4:1–6",
     "4. Historical Context Helps Us Understand Christian Teaching",
     "The language of Nicaea emerged in response to a specific fourth-century controversy. Understanding that context helps explain why particular terms became important.",
     "Key Scripture: Proverbs 18:13",
     "5. Political Power Can Complicate Religious Decisions",
     "Constantine supported the council partly because he wanted unity in the empire. Imperial involvement also contributed to coercion and political conflict in the years that followed.",
     "Key Scripture: Acts 5:29",
     "6. The Incarnation Is Essential to the Christian Story",
