   "B. Constantine XI",
   "C. Nero alone",
   "D. Justinian II",
   "12. Which statement best describes Basil’s approach to education?",
   "A. Education should be abandoned by all Christians.",
   "B. Education can be used to serve God and others.",
   "C. Education is more important than character.",
   "D. Only church leaders should learn to read.",
   "13. What is one important principle of servant leadership?",
   "A. Using authority to gain personal privilege",
   "B. Avoiding accountability",
   "C. Serving others with responsibility and humility",
   "D. Refusing to listen to criticism",
   "14. Why is organisation important in charitable work?",
   "A. It guarantees that every social problem will disappear.",
   "B. It helps communities direct resources and assistance toward genuine needs.",
   "C. It removes the need for compassion.",
   "D. It makes volunteers unnecessary.",
   "15. Which statement best summarises Basil’s legacy?",
   "A. Christian faith should concern only intellectual debate.",
   "B. Christian service should be separated from theology.",
   "C. Theology, spiritual discipline, leadership, and practical compassion can work together.",
   "D. A Christian leader’s main responsibility is personal recognition.",
   "PART B — SHORT-ANSWER QUESTIONS",
   "1. Who was Basil the Great?",
   "2. How did Basil’s family influence his Christian life?",
   "3. Why did Basil become interested in Christian communal life?",
   "4. What responsibilities did Basil carry as bishop of Caesarea?",
   "5. Why did Basil challenge selfish attitudes toward wealth?",
   "6. What was the Basiliad?",
   "7. How did Basil connect theology with practical service?",
   "8. What can modern churches learn from Basil’s charitable work?",
   "9. Why is Macrina the Younger important to Basil’s story?",
   "10. How can Christians build a lasting legacy of service?",
   "PART C — DEEPER REFLECTION QUESTIONS",
   "1. How can a person use education and professional skills to serve God and others?",
   "Suggested Reflection: Education can provide knowledge and abilities that help address real needs. A Christian can use professional skills to teach, solve problems, support charitable work, strengthen communities, and serve people with integrity. The key is to treat knowledge as a responsibility rather than merely a source of status.",
   "2. What does Basil’s example teach about the relationship between wealth and responsibility?",
   "Suggested Reflection: Basil challenged the idea that possessions should be used only for personal comfort. His teaching encourages Christians to consider whether their resources are being used wisely and whether they are responding to people experiencing hardship. Generosity should be practical, thoughtful, and respectful.",
   "3. Why is organised compassion important for a church or ministry?",
   "Suggested Reflection: Good intentions are not enough when people need continuing assistance. A church may need to identify needs, organise volunteers, manage resources, establish partnerships, and maintain accountability. Organisation helps ensure that compassion becomes reliable service rather than a temporary emotional response.",
   "4. How can Christian leaders combine courage with humility?",
   "Suggested Reflection: Christian leaders should remain faithful to their convictions while recognising that they can make mistakes. Courage allows them to resist improper pressure, while humility helps them listen, seek advice, accept correction, and treat others respectfully.",
   "5. What is the difference between helping people and controlling them?",
   "Suggested Reflection: Genuine help seeks the welfare and dignity of the person receiving assistance. Controlling behaviour uses assistance to demand inappropriate loyalty, manipulate decisions, or gain power. Christian service should empower people and respect their dignity rather than exploit vulnerability.",
   "6. How can prayer and practical service strengthen one another?",
   "Suggested Reflection: Prayer can deepen compassion, strengthen perseverance, and help believers examine their motives. Practical service allows faith to become visible in everyday life. Together, they can help Christians grow in love, humility, and responsibility.",
   "7. Why should a church recognise people whose service is not publicly visible?",
   "Suggested Reflection: Communities depend on many forms of service, including hospitality, administration, cleaning, caring for children, visiting the sick, and supporting people privately. Public recognition does not determine the value of a contribution. Every responsible act of service can strengthen the community.",
   "8. What kind of Christian legacy would you like to leave behind?",
   "Suggested Reflection: A meaningful legacy may include people who have been encouraged, knowledge that has been passed on, needs that have been addressed, and communities that have become stronger. The reflection should identify specific ways faith can influence relationships, work, and service."
