     "The theological significance of the council extended beyond the resolution of individual disputes. The Church was seeking to explain its understanding of the one God revealed as Father, Son, and Holy Spirit while remaining faithful to Scripture and the apostolic tradition.",
     "Gregory’s participation in the theological life of this era illustrates how careful thinking can serve the wider Christian community.",
     "The questions under discussion were not merely exercises for scholars. They affected worship, teaching, baptismal confession, and the Church’s understanding of the God it proclaimed.",
     "At the same time, the council took place within the political structures of the Roman Empire. The relationship between imperial authority and Church decisions could be complicated, and the historical development of Christian doctrine cannot be understood without considering both theological argument and political circumstances.",
     "Gregory’s importance lay in his theological contribution, not in the claim that he single-handedly settled every question. He worked alongside other bishops and theologians whose efforts helped shape the Church’s language about the Trinity.",
