     "John preached a series of sermons commonly known as Homilies on the Statues. These sermons addressed the people’s fear, their moral responsibilities, and the importance of repentance.",
     "He encouraged his listeners to remain grounded in faith rather than surrendering to panic. He also urged them to examine their lives and recognize that spiritual responsibility did not disappear during a public emergency.",
     "John’s sermons are valuable historical evidence because they reveal how a Christian preacher addressed a community under political pressure.",
     "The episode also illustrates the role of religious leadership during a crisis. People often need more than information when they face uncertainty. They need calm guidance, moral clarity, practical encouragement, and reminders of what remains important.",
     "At the same time, the crisis should not be simplified into a story in which preaching alone solved the city’s problems. Imperial officials, civic leaders, negotiations, and the wider political situation also influenced the outcome.",
