     "2. A meaningful legacy is built through service, character, and truthfulness—not merely fame.",
     "Practical Application",
     "Choose one area of your life in which your words or actions influence others. Commit to using that influence more responsibly during the next 30 days. Set a practical goal, identify someone who can encourage you, and review your progress at the end of the month.",
     "Kingdom Lessons — What John Chrysostom Teaches Us",
     "1. Words carry responsibility. The ability to speak persuasively should be used to communicate truth, encourage wisdom, and serve others rather than manipulate people.",
     "2. Scripture must be understood carefully. Effective Christian teaching requires attention to biblical context, meaning, and practical application.",
     "3. Worship should influence everyday life. Prayer, preaching, and participation in church should lead toward love, integrity, generosity, and obedience.",
     "4. Wealth creates moral responsibilities. Material resources should not become an excuse for pride or indifference to people in need.",
     "5. Christian leadership is service. A position of authority is an opportunity to care for others, manage resources responsibly, and promote the good of the community.",
     "6. Power does not remove accountability. Influential people should be held to moral standards, but criticism must remain truthful, proportionate, and fair.",
     "7. Courage requires wisdom. Speaking against wrongdoing is important, but responsible communication should avoid unnecessary hostility and unsupported accusations.",
     "8. Suffering does not eliminate every opportunity to serve. Even during exile, John continued to encourage people through letters and pastoral concern.",
     "9. Christian history requires honest examination. We can recognize a theologian’s contributions while also confronting harmful attitudes and limitations in their writings.",
     "10. Knowledge should produce transformation. The goal of learning Scripture is not merely to know more but to become more faithful in character and conduct.",
     "11. Compassion should become practical. Concern for the poor and vulnerable must lead to concrete action rather than remain a subject of sermons alone.",
     "12. A lasting legacy is built through service. Christian influence is most valuable when it helps others pursue truth, justice, mercy, and faithful discipleship."
