     "His influence continued after his death. His writings were read by later Christian leaders, and his role in the life of Augustine helped connect his ministry to one of the most influential theologians in Western Christianity.",
     "Yet Ambrose’s significance does not depend on treating him as a perfect man. Like other historical Christian leaders, he must be understood within the circumstances of his time. Some aspects of his ministry reflect enduring biblical concerns, while others require careful historical evaluation.",
     "His life offers a compelling example of a person whose public career took an unexpected direction and whose abilities were redirected toward Christian service.",
