   "In your response, discuss:",
   "• The responsibility of political leaders.",
   "• The responsibility of Christian leaders.",
   "• The relationship between authority and moral accountability.",
   "• The importance of repentance when wrongdoing has occurred.",
   "Part 3: Biblical Connection",
   "Read Acts 5:27–32 and 2 Samuel 12:1–13.",
   "Explain how these passages relate to the principle that human authority does not eliminate accountability to God.",
   "Identify one similarity and one difference between the biblical examples and Ambrose’s historical circumstances.",
   "Part 4: Personal Application",
   "Describe a situation in which you might need courage to uphold a moral or Christian conviction.",
   "Explain how you could respond with truthfulness, humility, wisdom, and respect for others.",
   "Part 5: Legacy Statement",
   "Write a personal statement of approximately 150–250 words answering this question:",
   "What kind of Christian influence do I want to leave behind, and what must I begin doing today to build that legacy?",
   "Part 6: Prayer and Commitment",
   "Write a prayer asking God to develop in you the courage to stand for truth, the humility to accept correction, the wisdom to lead responsibly, and the compassion to serve others.",
   "Conclude with one specific action you will take during the coming week to put these lessons into practice.",
   "Closing Prayer",
   "Heavenly Father,",
   "Thank You for the life and historical witness of Ambrose of Milan. Thank You for reminding us through his story that leadership is a responsibility to be carried with humility, wisdom, courage, and faithfulness.",
   "Lord, teach us to use our abilities and opportunities in ways that honor You. Help us to remain teachable when we lack understanding, disciplined when preparation is required, and faithful when difficult responsibilities come into our lives.",
   "Give us the courage to stand for truth without becoming proud, aggressive, or self-righteous. Teach us to speak with wisdom when confronting wrongdoing and to remember that our purpose should be to uphold what is right, protect those who are vulnerable, and encourage genuine repentance.",
   "Father, help those who hold positions of authority to recognize their responsibilities. May leaders in the church, government, families, schools, workplaces, and communities understand that influence is not a privilege for personal ambition but an opportunity to serve.",
   "Give us compassionate hearts toward the poor, the overlooked, and those who are suffering. Teach us to use our resources generously and our words constructively.",
   "Help us to become faithful students of Your Word. May our knowledge lead to obedience, our worship strengthen our faith, and our relationships become opportunities to encourage others in their spiritual journeys.",
   "When we make mistakes, give us the humility to acknowledge them and the courage to accept responsibility. When others correct us, help us to listen honestly rather than allowing pride to close our hearts.",
   "Lord, let our lives produce fruit that continues beyond our own generation. May the people we teach, encourage, support, and serve become stronger in faith and better equipped to serve others.",
   "Above all, help us to remember that our ultimate responsibility is to You. May we never exchange truth for popularity, justice for convenience, or faithfulness for personal advancement.",
   "Shape us into servants who lead through example, speak with integrity, act with compassion, and remain faithful to You in both public and private life.",
   "In the mighty name of Jesus Christ, we pray.",
   "Amen."
