     "Scripture Focus: Exodus 3:1–12; Exodus 33:12–23; Hebrews 11:23–29",
     "One of Gregory of Nyssa's most important works was The Life of Moses. Rather than simply recounting the biblical events of Moses' life, Gregory explored their spiritual significance.",
     "He presented Moses' journey as a pattern for the believer's growth toward God. Moses encountered God in the burning bush, confronted Pharaoh, led Israel out of Egypt, and received the law. Later, he ascended Mount Sinai and experienced a profound encounter with God's presence.",
     "Gregory interpreted these events as more than historical milestones. They also provided images of the spiritual journey.",
     "Leaving Egypt could represent turning away from slavery to sin and disordered desires. Crossing the wilderness could represent the difficulties of spiritual formation. Ascending the mountain could represent the continuing pursuit of a deeper knowledge of God.",
