     "The accusation carried enormous weight. Scriptures were central to Christian worship and teaching. Handing them over to authorities could be understood as an act of betrayal against the Christian community.",
     "However, the circumstances surrounding these accusations were not always simple. Different people had acted under different pressures, and disputes arose over what individuals had actually done.",
     "The question was no longer simply whether Christians should remain faithful during persecution. It had become a question about the future of those who had failed.",
