     "A group of younger members had challenged certain leaders, creating division within the congregation.",
     "A Christian leader in Rome, commonly known as Clement of Rome, wrote a letter to the Corinthians urging them to restore peace and order.",
     "The work, traditionally called 1 Clement, is one of the earliest surviving Christian writings outside the New Testament.",
     "Clement appealed to Scripture, the example of earlier believers, and the need for humility. He reminded the Corinthians that jealousy, pride, and rivalry had damaged relationships among God's people.",
     "He also emphasized that Christian ministry should be exercised responsibly and that the community should avoid unnecessary division.",
     "His letter illustrates how early Christian leaders used the Scriptures to address practical problems.",
