     "His approach was influenced partly by the interpretive traditions of Alexandria and by the philosophical methods used in the wider intellectual world.",
     "Origen believed that Scripture could lead readers toward deeper spiritual understanding. He sometimes interpreted biblical narratives figuratively when he thought a purely literal reading failed to explain the passage adequately.",
     "For example, he might seek a spiritual lesson in a biblical event beyond its immediate historical meaning.",
     "This approach influenced later Christian interpreters, but it also generated controversy.",
