     "John Chrysostom, who served in Antioch before becoming bishop of Constantinople, became famous for his detailed preaching and explanation of biblical texts.",
     "The Antiochene emphasis helped guard against interpretations that ignored the passage's actual meaning.",
     "However, historical and literary attention alone does not eliminate every interpretive difficulty. Readers must still consider theological themes and the relationship between different parts of Scripture.",
