     "When Paul travelled to Corinth, he met Priscilla and Aquila, and they worked together because they shared the same occupation.",
     "Their relationship developed beyond business. They became fellow workers in Christian ministry.",
     "Priscilla and Aquila later travelled with Paul and settled in Ephesus.",
     "There they encountered Apollos, an eloquent speaker who knew the Scriptures and taught about Jesus with enthusiasm. However, his understanding of the Christian message was incomplete.",
     "Acts records that Priscilla and Aquila heard him speaking and took him aside. Together, they explained the way of God to him more accurately.",
     "This account is particularly important because it explicitly identifies Priscilla as participating in the instruction of another Christian teacher.",
     "The passage does not provide a transcript of their conversation, but it clearly presents both Priscilla and Aquila as involved in helping Apollos develop a more accurate understanding.",
     "Their approach also offers a valuable lesson in how correction can be given.",
     "They did not publicly humiliate Apollos. Instead, they took him aside and explained what he needed to understand.",
     "Apollos subsequently became an effective Christian teacher, serving in different regions and helping believers through his knowledge of the Scriptures.",
     "Priscilla and Aquila's contribution illustrates the importance of accurate teaching, shared ministry, and personal discipleship.",
     "It also reminds us that effective teachers need to remain willing to learn.",
