     "The passage also records that they had a disagreement. Paul urged them to agree in the Lord and asked a trusted companion to help them.",
     "This brief account shows both the significance of their contribution and the reality that faithful Christian workers can experience conflict.",
     "Their disagreement did not erase Paul's recognition of their labour in the gospel. At the same time, their ministry did not exempt them from the responsibility to pursue reconciliation.",
     "Romans 16 names several other women who were associated with the work of the early Church.",
     "Mary is commended for working hard among the Roman believers. Tryphena and Tryphosa are described as workers in the Lord. Persis is commended for her hard work.",
     "These references may appear brief, but together they reveal a much wider picture of early Christian ministry.",
     "Paul did not describe the growth of the Church as the achievement of one missionary acting alone. He recognized a community of people whose work supported the proclamation of the gospel.",
